// blessed: vrs -- builds next frame's shading rate image for the lit pass from its colour and motion (fidelityfx variable shading, ported).
//
// One 8x8 workgroup per 16x16 rate tile, each thread one 2x2 coarse pixel,
// base rates only (1x1, 1x2, 2x1, 2x2). A straight port of
// VrsGenerateVrsImage for FFX_VARIABLESHADING_TILESIZE 16 from the
// FidelityFX SDK (sdk/include/FidelityFX/gpu/vrs/ffx_variable_shading.h,
// release-FSR3-3.0.4), with these changes:
// - luminance comes from the lit pass's hdr colour, mapped to a display-like
//   range with sqrt(l / (1 + l)), not from a tonemapped frame;
// - motion comes as prevUV - currUV (skyrim's convention), converted to the
//   ffx convention (current - previous, in pixels); the (1,0) sentinel and
//   anything over half a screen count as no motion;
// - the tile maximum uses shared atomics instead of subgroup max + and;
// - a two-frame hysteresis: a tile goes coarse on an axis only when this
//   frame and the last both asked for it, and back to 1x1 at once.
//
